{
  "case": "render.layout.io-link-rerouted",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a79.4 Region geometry, including Process IO",
  "witness": "links incident to a relocated region item are routed after expansion; their route members are UNSEALED and checked by the LINK-ROUTE invariants",
  "derivation": "A BPMNEdge for Assoc_A1 touches In_A, which the region rule moves to (132000,15000,36000,50000). DESIGN \u00a79.4 'Route all links after expansion' defines no routing rule, so the adapter routes (the Python adapter uses the two-point centre route, shown) and the case leaves the edge waypoints and bounds and the page bounds UNSEALED (harmonization K5, R3.4 erratum E-11): the LINK-ROUTE invariants are checked instead (at least two waypoints, first inside or on the final source bounds, last inside or on the final target bounds, bounds equal to the waypoint bounding box, endpoints In_A_di -> Task_1_di unchanged); every other member is exact and equals render.layout.io-anchored. Row rule (spec \u00a74.3): items in \u00a77.2 placement order; footprint max(object, label) width; left = anchor centre - footprint/2 when the anchor is shown, else contentLeft or previous right + gap; clamp to contentLeft; collision shifts right; one row at the top of the support body [Ly, Ly+RH], RH = max(minHeight, max(object+label) + 2 padding) (harmonization K2); every object centre lies on one line cy = Ly + max(A, (RH + A - B)/2), A = max h/2, B = max(h/2 + label height), so the union of the stacks is centred in the row (DESIGN \u00a79.4 'align centers on one IO row'); exact rationals, one roundEven per output coordinate. The profile is re-pinned to the lot-4 extension packages neutral-render-descriptors/1 and neutral-render-base/1 (tests/profile_render/expected/artifacts/), which admit every native type of the tree.",
